39:with latched backstops, so these lines describe the unfixed tree only:
40:
41:    cpu_arm.c:606-608   arm_load_register_bank: default: fatal("...unimplemented mode %i"); exit(1);
42:    cpu_arm.c:559-561   arm_save_register_bank: default: same
43:
44:`0xE321F014' is `MSR CPSR_c, #0x14' -- mode 0x14 is a RESERVED ARM mode, so the Load arm's
45:`default:' is reached and the process dies.  `%i' prints DECIMAL: `unimplemented mode 20'.
46:
47:*** POLARITY: WANT IS POST-FIX CORRECT.  A PRE FAIL ON A DEFECT ROW *IS* THE REPRODUCTION. ***
48:*** ORACLE: EOF ALONE => DEAD.  THE TEXT IS DIAGNOSIS, NEVER HALF THE TRIGGER. ***
49:
50:#562 THE FIX AND WHAT THIS PROBE NOW DETECTS.  Three guest writers can put an unmodelled mode
51:(anything but 10 11 12 13 17 1b 1f) into CPSR, and each now DECLINES THE MODE FIELD ONLY, with a
52:`(once)' announce naming its site: msr_imm (`MSR CPSR_c'), arm_pop's `LDM {..pc}^' SPSR restore,
53:and the DPI S-to-PC SPSR restore (`MOVS pc,..', `SUBS pc,lr,..').  The restores keep the CURRENT
54:mode in M[4:0] and assign every other bit from the SPSR (DPI later forces T for an odd destination
55:PC; not driven here).  The Save/Load `default:' arms are BACKSTOPS (latched announce, return, no
56:exit(1)), reached only once an unmodelled mode is ALREADY in CPSR, which no guest instruction can
57:now install -- only a debugger `cpsr=' assignment.  After such a plant Save's default: is reached
58:by a guest `MSR CPSR_c' to a modelled mode (dbg save), a DPI S-to-PC (dbg both, latch rpt) or
59:exception entry; Load's default: ONLY by a DPI S-to-PC executed in the planted mode (dbg both,
60:latch rpt).  An `LDM {..pc}^' from a planted mode stops the CPU at arm_pop's selector default:
61:first (pre-existing; not this fix).  POST-FIX the guest is in SVC32 with the I/F bits the write
62:set -- `#0x14' clears I and F -- NOT in a reserved mode.  Rows added by #562: kill 1e, kill 03,
63:rst movs, rst ldm, zero spsr, acc movs, acc ldm, dbg save, dbg both, latch ind, latch rpt, src
64:dpi/src pop x {fiq irq abt und svc}, msr lbl, encl, tbit, encl2, msr wide, grid msr, grid dpi,
65:grid pop, grid cov, the `if=' (I/F) pin on
66:kill 14 / kill 15, and ` sp0' (an actual zero SP readback) on the rows whose SP is a never-loaded
67:bank.
68:
69:MODES 0x00-0x0F ARE NOW CLAIMED.  This header used to BAN `MSR CPSR_c, #0' as "the 26-bit hole,
70:a different defect".  The helper declines 0x00-0x0F like any other unmodelled value, and
71:`zero spsr' drives exactly mode 0x00 (an SPSR never written is zero: cpu_new zero-fills).
72:
73:THE GENERATED GRID (repair 5; owner ruling 2026-10-08).  The restore/MSR coverage is GENERATED
74:from tables (grid_obs(): labels, MODELLED, UNMODELLED, complementary value pairs), not written row
75:by row: `grid msr', `grid dpi', `grid pop' run every generated observation and compare the WHOLE
76:CPSR word; `grid cov' re-derives the G1 table (outcome x bit x polarity, aggregated over labels and
77:latch states) from the same generator and reds on any uncovered G1 cell.  G2, G3 and G4 hold by the
78:generator's construction (counted statically on the final pass: G2 80 of 80 label x bit cells, G3
79:96 of 96, G4 8 of 8), NOT by a row -- `grid cov' does not assert them.
80:  G1 every (path, outcome, bit 0..31, polarity) cell has an observation whose result bit DIFFERS
81:     from the wrong source -- OLD's bit for every non-mode bit and for an accept's mode bits; NEW's
82:     (the SPSR / operand's) bit for a DECLINE's mode bits, which must equal the LABEL.  Complementary
83:     pairs: p1 OLD = label (bits 31:5 clear) / NEW = 0xffffffe0 | mode (31:5 set, T SET); p2 OLD =
84:     0xffffffc0 | label (31:6 set, T clear) / NEW = mode (31:5 clear) -- so keep-old, force-0 and
85:     force-1 all change the word.  This is a UNION across observations, not a property of every
86:     decline.  (Repair 5's text said the result "must equal the SPSR / operand value while the OLD
87:     CPSR's bit differs (OLD 0 / NEW all-ones-with-T, and OLD all-ones / NEW 0)": FALSE for a
88:     decline's mode bits and for both pairs' OLD values; corrected 2026-10-09 from grok's and
89:     codex's final-pass readings, against grid_obs() and grid_cov().)
90:     Named equivalents: bit 4 polarity 0 and bit 4 on accept (every modelled mode and label
91:     has bit 4 set, so keep-old / force-1 equal the right answer there), and T
92:     polarity 0 against OLD T = 1 (the guest runs ARM code, so OLD T is always 0; keep-old T is
93:     caught at polarity 1).  The latch is SET for every decline after a session's first.
94:  G2 every msr_imm label (FIQ IRQ SVC ABT UND SYS) declines label ^ 0x1f, which differs in all
95:     five mode bits; the restore labels decline the same value as the SPSR.
96:  G3 all 25 unmodelled values are declined and all 7 modelled modes accepted on EACH path.
97:  G4 arm_pop's enclosing cells {S, non-S} x {PC, no PC}, all four, in grid pop.
98:  The hand-written rows below remain (G5): label x latch x outcome (src), tbit (T with the latch
99:  clear, by `print cpsr'), encl / encl2 (the DPI enclosing cells), msr wide, msr lbl.  Sessions:
100:  the probe prints ARMMSRMODE_SESSIONS.
101:
102:CONTRACT (floor clause (e)) -- the edits this detector is DESIGNED to catch:
103:  * exit(1) reinstated at Save's default: (dbg save, dbg both, latch rpt) or Load's (dbg both,
104:    latch rpt);
105:  * the helper answering 1 always (kill 14/15/1e), wrong on ANY of the 32 mode values on ANY path
106:    -- narrowed (e.g. `& 0x17' admits 0x18-0x1a), widened by any bit 31:5, or dropped (grid *:
107:    G3 drives all 25 unmodelled and all 7 modelled values through each path; src rows, tbit,
108:    msr wide);
109:  * the guard dropped at msr_imm (kill rows), arm_pop (rst ldm, src pop x FIQ IRQ ABT UND SVC) or
110:    DPI (rst movs, zero spsr, src dpi x FIQ IRQ ABT UND SVC), or restricted to ONE label, or to
111:    one unmodelled value such as 0x14 (src rows decline 0x0f), or compiled into the MOV instance
112:    only (encl2: `subs pc,lr');
113:  * the msr_imm guard skipped at one current-mode label (msr lbl: a decline from each of FIQ IRQ
114:    ABT UND SYS; latch rpt: SVC with the latch set);
115:  * the msr_imm decline clearing fewer than all five mode bits at ANY label (grid msr: G2
116:    declines label ^ 0x1f at all six labels; kill 03, encl2), or clearing MORE (`& ~0x3f', T lost:
117:    tbit, grid msr); the restore keep-mode mask letting any SPSR mode bit through (grid dpi/pop:
118:    G2; src rows);
119:  * a restore guard made unconditional, or unconditional for one label, or skipped / forced for one
120:    label x latch-state cell (src rows: all 40 cells; acc movs, acc ldm);
121:  * a WHOLE-OPERATION decline in msr_imm instead of field-only (the `if=' pin on kill rows; msr
122:    wide);
123:  * a decline OR accept taking ANY bit 31:5 from the old CPSR, or forcing it to 0 or to 1, with
124:    the latch SET (grid G1); with the latch CLEAR the restore paths are observed only with SPSR
125:    bits 31:8 SET (grid obs 0, src R2) -- a force-1 or OR-old of bits 31:8 on a FIRST DPI/pop
126:    decline, or a force-1 on a latch-clear restore accept, is NOT CLAIMED (MEASURED 47/47 on the
127:    final pass: N_pop_forceN_first, N_dpi_forceN_first, N_pop_orold_first, N_dpi_orold_first,
128:    E_pop_forceN_clracc -- artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/); on msr the
129:    latch-clear decline is held by msr wide ALONE and the latch-clear accept by grid pop's G4 p1
130:    cells ALONE.  (Repair 5's text claimed "with the latch clear or set (grid *: G1 complementary
131:    pairs; src R2/R3; tbit; msr wide)": FALSE for bits 31:8 at the restores; narrowed 2026-10-09,
132:    owner ruling, the Opus 5.5 seat's measurement and suggested text.) --
133:    this replaces the repair-3 sentence "the declined SPSR has N Z I F SET while the CPSR it
134:    replaces has them CLEAR" (FALSE for N and Z) and repair 4's "at EVERY decline, every restored
135:    bit differs" (FALSE for T at src R2/R3 and msr wide: it held only as a UNION);
136:  * any two of the five latch sites sharing a bit (latch rpt: all five in one process; also
137:    dbg both, latch ind);
138:  * a latch that never SUPPRESSES (`|=' -> `&=', or the `|=' line deleted), or a repair applied
139:    only while its latch is clear (latch rpt: every site visited TWICE; src rows per label);
140:  * the enclosing predicates widened in ANY of their cells: arm_pop's `if (return_flag)' (grid
141:    pop: all four {S, non-S} x {PC, no PC}; also encl, encl2), the DPI template's
142:    `rd == PC' compare (encl: non-S `add r0,pc'; encl2: S `adds r0,pc'), and the restore's
143:    `#ifdef A__S' (encl: non-S `add pc,r6,#0' -- NOT `mov pc,lr', which the decoder turns into
144:    `ret' and so never reaches the DPI template).
145:NOT CLAIMED, disclosed: DPI opcode instances other than MOV and SUB (graded (e): the opcode
146:flows into nothing the repair reads).  The msr_imm comment's "only the LOCAL mask changes:
147:ic->arg[] is a cached translation" is NOT pinned, in either form.  Every re-execution in this
148:probe follows a debugger INTERACTION (to set r1, or to dump), and debugger() clears every dyntrans
149:translation when it interacts (src/debugger/debugger.c, "Clear all dyntrans translations"; it
150:returns before that clear only while a `step N' count or a `step call' is still running, and this
151:probe re-executes an instruction only across an interaction), so each execution is
152:re-translated from the instruction word and a write to ic->arg[] never reaches the next one.
153:MEASURED: M_msr_argmask -- the decline also writes `ic->arg[1] &= ~ARM_FLAG_MODE' -- scores 47/47
154:(artifacts/armmsrmodekill/killtable5_20261008/kt1b/).  Repair 5's text said the grid's
155:re-executions of `msr cpsr_fsxc,r1' pinned the register form: FALSE, for that reason (corrected
156:2026-10-09).  A guest LOOP that re-executes ONE translated MSR inside a single `step N', changing
157:the register between passes, pins it -- measured in the filed prototype (opus_pass2r5_20261009/
158:probe48.py, a 48-row probe: fix 48/48, M_msr_argmask 47/48, KTR5_LANE5.out); not included here.  The LATCH-CLEAR cells the latch-set grid
159:does not reach: msr has no latch-clear decline at IRQ, ABT, UND or SYS (msr lbl's first decline is
160:FIQ's), and the restores' latch-clear mode-bit cells at IRQ/bit 1, ABT/bits 0-2 and UND/bits 0,1,3
161:are unobserved -- MEASURED 47/47: M_msr_clr0f_irq_first, M_msr_skip_irq_first
162:(opus_pass2r5_20261009/KTR5_LANE4.out); with the bits 31:8 cells above, filed as one follow-up row with a measured closure (a
163:zero-observation reorder of the restore grid sessions) and the loop row.  Per-CPU latch isolation
164:(one CPU only); exception entry as a
165:Save-backstop route (no row); T-bit / execution-state coherence after a T-set restore beyond the
166:CPSR word itself; the USR/SYS `LDM {pc}^' and `MSR SPSR' paths that stop the CPU (filed
167:separately).  The grid, tbit and `print cpsr' readbacks are rung-3 debugger observations.  The
168:`msr wide' accept 0xffffffd1 sets operand bits 31:6, 4 and 0 only (bits 3:1 are clear: the grid's
169:accepts and c_17 / c_1b / c_1f carry them) -- repair 4's header said "bits 31:6, 4:0".
170:
171:NAMED-RED tally: HEAD = 18/47, RED exactly the 29 rows kill 14, kill 15, save 2s, kill 1e,
172:kill 03, rst movs, rst ldm, zero spsr, dbg save, dbg both, latch ind, latch rpt, the ten src *
173:rows, msr lbl, tbit, encl2, msr wide, grid msr, grid dpi, grid pop, CONTROL=OK.  `encl' drives no
174:unmodelled mode and `grid cov' is static, so both are GREEN on HEAD.  `save 2s' on HEAD is the
175:SAME Load death as `kill 14' (EOF on the first MSR) -- it is not an independent HEAD reproduction
176:of Save; nor is `dbg both' a HEAD reproduction of Load (HEAD dies in Save first).  47/47 on HEAD
177:is a broken vehicle, not success.
178:
179:Stay on `step', never `continue' (IRQ dispatch is inside `if (!single_step)').
180:"""
181:import os
182:import pty
183:import re
184:import select
185:import signal
186:import sys
187:import time
188:
189:BIN = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "../build/gxemul"
190:LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"
191:
192:STUB = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "arm_bfx_stub.bin")
193:if not os.path.exists(STUB):
194:    with open(STUB, "wb") as f:
195:        f.write(b"\0" * 16)
196:
197:CODE = 0x8000
198:DEST = 0x9000
199:BOOT_SP = 0x03FFF000
200:BOOT_CPSR = 0xD3
201:POISON = 0xDEADBEEF
202:MARK = "@MARK"
203:
204:#  *** ONE WORDS DICT.  Every `put w' is drawn from here and every MSR session dumps its whole
205:#  planted stream against these entries before the stimulus (R4). ***
206:WORDS = {
207:    "mrs_r3":   0xE10F3000,              # mrs  r3, cpsr
208:    "str_r3":   0xE5843000,              # str  r3, [r4]
209:    "str_r3_4": 0xE5843004,              # str  r3, [r4,#4]
210:    "str_r3_8": 0xE5843008,              # str  r3, [r4,#8]
211:    "str_r3_c": 0xE584300C,              # str  r3, [r4,#12]
212:    "str_sp_8": 0xE584D008,              # str  r13,[r4,#8]
213:    "str_sp_c": 0xE584D00C,              # str  r13,[r4,#12]
214:    "str_sp_10": 0xE584D010,             # str  r13,[r4,#16]
215:    "mov_r0_2a": 0xE3A0002A,             # mov  r0, #0x2a
216:    "str_r0":   0xE5840000,              # str  r0, [r4]
217:    "b_self":   0xEAFFFFFE,              # b    .
218:}
219:for m in (0x03, 0x10, 0x11, 0x12, 0x13, 0x14, 0x15, 0x17, 0x1B, 0x1E, 0x1F):
220:    WORDS["c_%02x" % m] = 0xE321F000 | m     # msr cpsr_c, #m
221:WORDS["f_14"] = 0xE328F014                   # msr cpsr_f, #0x14
222:#  #562: SPSR poisoning and the two restore paths.
223:for m in (0x14, 0x1F):
224:    WORDS["s_%02x" % m] = 0xE361F000 | m     # msr spsr_c, #m
225:WORDS["movs_pc_lr"] = 0xE1B0F00E             # movs pc, lr       (DPI S-to-PC restore)
226:WORDS["ldm_r5_pc_s"] = 0xE8D58000            # ldmia r5, {pc}^   (arm_pop restore)
227:
228:TGT = 0x8100                                 # restore target: lr, and the word at LDMW
229:LDMW = 0x9100                                # where `ldm_r5_pc_s' loads pc from
230:TGT_OPS = ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"]
231:TGT2 = 0x8140                                # `latch ind': readback after the chained MOVS
232:#  #562 pass 2: words for `latch rpt' and the `src *' rows.
233:WORDS["ldm_r6_pc_s"] = 0xE8D68000            # ldmia r6, {pc}^
234:WORDS["mov_lr_8100"] = 0xE3A0EC81            # mov  lr, #0x8100  (0x81 ror 24)
235:WORDS["add_lr_40"] = 0xE28EE040              # add  lr, lr, #0x40
236:WORDS["sf_c0"] = 0xE368F103                  # msr  spsr_f, #0xc0000000  (N and Z; 0x03 ror 2)
237:NZ = 0xC0000000
238:#  #562 repair 3: label entry WITH I and F set, the class-closure SPSR values, the chained-restore
239:#  operands, and the enclosing-predicate controls.
240:for m in (0xD1, 0xD2, 0xD3, 0xD7, 0xDB, 0xDF):
241:    WORDS["c_%02x" % m] = 0xE321F000 | m     # msr cpsr_c, #m  (I|F|mode)
242:for m in (0xCF, 0xDF):
243:    WORDS["s_%02x" % m] = 0xE361F000 | m     # msr spsr_c, #m
244:WORDS["movs_pc_r5"] = 0xE1B0F005             # movs pc, r5        (DPI S-to-PC; r5 is not banked)
245:WORDS["add_r5_40"] = 0xE2855040              # add  r5, r5, #0x40
246:WORDS["ldm_r6w_pc_s"] = 0xE8F68000           # ldmia r6!, {pc}^   (arm_pop restore, chained)
247:WORDS["ldm_r5_pc"] = 0xE8958000              # ldmia r5, {pc}     (NO ^: return_flag stays 0)
248:WORDS["add_pc_r6_0"] = 0xE286F000            # add  pc, r6, #0    (non-S DPI to PC; not `ret')
249:WORDS["add_r0_pc_0"] = 0xE28F0000            # add  r0, pc, #0    (Rn = PC, Rd != PC)
250:WORDS["str_r0_c"] = 0xE584000C               # str  r0, [r4,#12]
251:WORDS["str_r3_10"] = 0xE5843010              # str  r3, [r4,#16]
252:WORDS["str_r3_14"] = 0xE5843014              # str  r3, [r4,#20]
253:#  OPUS CLOSURE words
254:WORDS["msr_fsxc_r0"] = 0xE12FF000            # msr cpsr_fsxc, r0  (register form -> msr_imm)
255:WORDS["msr_fsxc_r1"] = 0xE12FF001            # msr cpsr_fsxc, r1
256:WORDS["adds_r0_pc_0"] = 0xE29F0000           # adds r0, pc, #0
257:WORDS["ldm_r5_r0_s"] = 0xE8D50001            # ldmia r5, {r0}^
258:WORDS["subs_pc_lr_0"] = 0xE25EF000           # subs pc, lr, #0
259:WORDS["sf_ff"] = 0xE368F4FF                  # msr spsr_f, #0xff000000
260:WORDS["ss_ff"] = 0xE364F8FF                  # msr spsr_s, #0x00ff0000
261:WORDS["sx_ff"] = 0xE362FCFF                  # msr spsr_x, #0x0000ff00
262:WORDS["cf_0"] = 0xE32EF000                   # msr cpsr_fsx, #0
263:for m in (0x3F, 0x34):
264:    WORDS["c_%02x" % m] = 0xE321F000 | m
265:    WORDS["s_%02x" % m] = 0xE361F000 | m
266:
267:rows = []
268:diagnosis = []
269:
270:
271:def row(name, got, want, note=""):
272:    rows.append((name, str(got), str(want), note))
273:
274:
275:NSESS = [0]
276:
277:
278:def session(cmds, settle=1.6, spin=1.6):
279:    """ONE FRESH PROCESS per scored row that executes a guest instruction.  Returns (t, alive);
280:    _session_split() turns the `@MARK' pseudo-command into the early/late split (R2)."""
281:    NSESS[0] += 1
282:    pid, fd = pty.fork()
283:    if pid == 0:
284:        os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-A", "-E", "testarm", "-M", "64",
285:                       "0x%x:%s" % (CODE, STUB)])
286:        os._exit(127)
287:    buf = ""
288:    eof = False
289:
290:    def rd(t):
291:        nonlocal buf, eof
292:        end = time.time() + t
293:        while time.time() < end:
294:            try:
295:                r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.1)
296:            except OSError:
297:                eof = True
298:                return
299:            if not r:
300:                continue
301:            try:
302:                d = os.read(fd, 65536)
303:            except OSError:
304:                eof = True
305:                return
306:            if not d:
307:                eof = True
308:                return
309:            buf += d.decode("utf-8", "replace")
310:
311:    rd(settle)
312:    for c in cmds:
313:        if eof:
314:            break
315:        try:
316:            os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode())
317:        except OSError:
318:            eof = True
319:            break
320:        rd(0.3)
321:    rd(spin)
322:
323:    #  *** POLL, NEVER SAMPLE ONCE. ***  rd() returns immediately on EOF, so a dying child must
324:    #  be given time to die.  On EOF reap with a long deadline; without EOF a short one (R7).
325:    alive = True
326:    deadline = time.time() + (12.0 if eof else 3.0)
327:    while time.time() < deadline:
328:        try:
329:            wpid, _st = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)
330:        except ChildProcessError:
331:            alive = False
332:            break
333:        if wpid == pid:
334:            alive = False
335:            break
336:        time.sleep(0.05)
337:    if alive:
338:        try:
339:            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)
340:        except OSError:
341:            pass
342:        try:
343:            _w, st = os.waitpid(pid, 0)
344:            #  R7: if the child exited on its own between the last poll and our kill, the
345:            #  status says so -- do not leave alive=True for a process that died by itself.
346:            if os.WIFEXITED(st) or (os.WIFSIGNALED(st) and os.WTERMSIG(st) != signal.SIGKILL):
347:                alive = False
348:        except ChildProcessError:
349:            pass
350:    try:
351:        os.close(fd)
352:    except OSError:
353:        pass
354:    return buf.replace("\r", ""), alive
355:
356:
357:def _session_split(cmds):
358:    #  Insert a unique, harmless marker command at MARK so the split survives \r stripping:
359:    #  `print 0x5eed5eed' is answered by the debugger (sh_intprio_probe.py measured `print
360:    #  0x1234'), and even if it were not, its echo carries the token.
361:    real = []
362:    for c in cmds:
363:        real.append("print 0x5eed5eed" if c == MARK else c)
364:    t, alive = session(real)
365:    i = t.find("5eed5eed")
366:    if i < 0:
367:        return t, "", alive, False
368:    #  late = everything after the marker's answer line (skip echo + answer)
369:    j = t.rfind("5eed5eed")
370:    nl = t.find("\n", j)
371:    late = t[nl + 1:] if nl >= 0 else ""
372:    return t[:i], late, alive, True
373:
374:
375:def printed(t, reg):
376:    #  COPIED VERBATIM from regress/lca_isalane_probe.py.  `print <reg>' emits a BARE `0x...'.
377:    m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
378:    return None if not m else int(m.group(1), 16)
379:
380:
381:def dumpcmd(addr, end=None):
382:    """*** ALWAYS DUMP FROM THE 16-BYTE-ALIGNED BASE. ***  debugger_cmd_dump does
383:    `addr = addr_start & ~0xf' and blank-pads groups before addr_start (arm_bdt_probe.py
384:    read_mem32(), measured 2026-09-11)."""
385:    base = addr & ~0xF
386:    top = ((end if end is not None else addr) + 16) & ~0xF
387:    if top <= base:
388:        top = base + 16
389:    return "dump 0x%x 0x%x" % (base, top)
390:
391:
392:def dumped(t, addr):
393:    """The word stored at `addr', from the LAST aligned dump line in `t' (R2: callers pass the
394:    early or the late half, never the whole transcript).  Memory-order bytes, little-endian
395:    guest: assemble like sw() in arm_flags_probe.py."""
396:    label = "0x%08x" % (addr & ~0xF)
397:    idx = (addr & 0xF) // 4
398:    val = None
399:    for line in t.splitlines():
400:        if line.startswith(label):
401:            parts = line[12:48].split()
402:            if len(parts) == 4 and len(parts[idx]) == 8:
403:                val = int.from_bytes(bytes.fromhex(parts[idx]), "little")
404:    return val
405:
406:
407:def plant(ops, at=CODE):
408:    out = []
409:    for i, k in enumerate(ops):
410:        out.append("put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * i, WORDS[k]))
411:    out.append("put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * len(ops), WORDS["b_self"]))
412:    return out
413:
414:
415:def prologue():
416:    """POISON DEST..DEST+16 (the post-MSR stores must overwrite them) and point r4 at DEST."""
417:    return ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (DEST + o, POISON) for o in (0, 4, 8, 12, 16)] \
418:        + ["r4=0x%x" % DEST]
419:
420:
421:PREFIX = ["mrs_r3", "str_r3"]
422:
423:
424:def msr_cmds(ops, steps_after, late_end=DEST + 12, restore=False, regs=(), poke=(),
425:             chain=False):
426:    """Standard MSR session: prefix MRS/STR to DEST, arming dumps (DEST and the whole planted
427:    stream), MARK, the stimulus steps, then the result dump.
428:    #562: restore=True also plants TGT_OPS at TGT, sets lr=TGT and the LDMW word to TGT, and
429:    arms all three (a fall-through past the restore lands on b_self and reads `nofire').
430:    `regs' are debugger assignments made BEFORE the prefix; `poke' ones AFTER the arming dumps
431:    (a `cpsr=' poke must follow the prefix, whose MRS arms DEST == 0xd3).
432:    chain=True (with restore): TGT holds `movs pc,lr' and the readback TGT_OPS move to TGT2,
433:    where lr points -- so one session can run an LDM^ restore and then a MOVS restore."""
434:    full = PREFIX + ops
435:    cmds = prologue() + plant(full)
436:    extra = {}
437:    rb = TGT2 if chain else TGT
438:    if restore:
439:        cmds += plant(TGT_OPS, at=rb) + ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (LDMW, TGT),
440:                                         "lr=0x%x" % rb, "r5=0x%x" % LDMW]
441:        for i, k in enumerate(TGT_OPS + ["b_self"]):
442:            extra[rb + 4 * i] = WORDS[k]
443:        extra[LDMW] = TGT
444:        if chain:
445:            cmds += plant(["movs_pc_lr"], at=TGT)
446:            extra[TGT] = WORDS["movs_pc_lr"]
447:            extra[TGT + 4] = WORDS["b_self"]
448:    cmds += list(regs) + ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step 2", dumpcmd(DEST),
449:                          dumpcmd(CODE, CODE + 4 * len(full))]
450:    if restore:
451:        cmds += [dumpcmd(TGT, TGT + 4 * len(TGT_OPS)), dumpcmd(LDMW)]
452:        if chain:
453:            cmds += [dumpcmd(TGT2, TGT2 + 4 * len(TGT_OPS))]
454:    cmds += [MARK] + list(poke) + ["step %d" % s for s in steps_after] \
455:        + [dumpcmd(DEST, late_end)]
456:    return cmds, (full, extra)
457:
458:
459:def arming(early, full):
460:    """R4: DEST == 0xd3 after the prefix, and every planted word reads back as its WORDS entry.
461:    #562: `full' may be (ops, {addr: word}) -- the extra plants (restore target, LDM word)."""
462:    extra = {}
463:    if isinstance(full, tuple):
464:        full, extra = full
465:    if dumped(early, DEST) != BOOT_CPSR:
466:        return False
467:    for i, k in enumerate(full):
468:        if dumped(early, CODE + 4 * i) != WORDS[k]:
469:            return False
470:    for a, w in extra.items():
471:        if dumped(early, a) != w:
472:            return False
473:    return True
474:
475:
476:def prog_session(code_ops, blocks=(), data=None, regs=(), segments=((), ()), late_end=DEST + 12):
477:    """#562 pass 2: a multi-block program.  code_ops at CODE (after PREFIX), each (addr, ops) block
478:    at addr, each {addr: word} data word planted; every block and data word is ARMED (dumped and
479:    checked before MARK).  `segments' = ((pokes, steps), ...) after MARK: debugger assignments,
480:    then `step N'."""
481:    data = data or {}
482:    full = PREFIX + list(code_ops)
483:    cmds = prologue() + plant(full)
484:    extra = {}
485:    for a, ops in blocks:
486:        cmds += plant(ops, at=a)
487:        for i, k in enumerate(list(ops) + ["b_self"]):
488:            extra[a + 4 * i] = WORDS[k]
489:    for a, w in data.items():
490:        cmds.append("put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (a, w))
491:        extra[a] = w
492:    cmds += list(regs) + ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step 2", dumpcmd(DEST),
493:                          dumpcmd(CODE, CODE + 4 * len(full))]
494:    for a, ops in blocks:
495:        cmds.append(dumpcmd(a, a + 4 * len(ops)))
496:    for a in data:
497:        cmds.append(dumpcmd(a))
498:    cmds.append(MARK)
499:    for pokes, steps in segments:
500:        cmds += list(pokes) + (["step %d" % steps] if steps else [])
501:    cmds.append(dumpcmd(DEST, late_end))
502:    early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
503:    return early, late, alive, marked, (full, extra)
504:
505:
506:def announces(t, key):
507:    """#562 pass 2: how MANY `(once)' lines the named site printed -- a latch that never
508:    suppresses prints twice when its site is visited twice; any() could not see that."""
509:    return sum(1 for ln in t.splitlines() if key in ln and "(once)" in ln)
510:
511:
512:def diag_unimpl(nm, t):
513:    """#562: which register-bank `unimplemented mode' text a session printed (HEAD: the
514:    function that exit(1)ed -- the reason under test; fixed: the backstop that announced)."""
515:    hits = sorted(set(re.findall(r"arm_(save|load)_register_bank: unimplemented mode (\d+)", t)))
516:    diagnosis.append("%s: %s" % (nm, ", ".join("%s mode %s" % h for h in hits) if hits
517:                                 else "no bank text"))
518:
519:
520:def announced(t, key):
521:    """#562: a `(once)' announce from the NAMED site -- the five sites share the token, so a
522:    bare `(once)' cannot tell a decline from a backstop, or Save's backstop from Load's."""
523:    return any(key in ln and "(once)" in ln for ln in t.splitlines())
524:
525:
526:def classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, cpsr_at=DEST + 4, sp_at=None, rt_at=None,
527:             once_key=None, pin_if=False, backstops=False, declines=False):
528:    """The got string.  EOF ALONE => dead.  Arming is checked first, from the EARLY half.
529:    #562: once_key names the announcing site; pin_if adds the CPSR I/F pair (field-only vs
530:    whole-operation decline); backstops adds ` save' / ` load' per Save/Load announce."""
531:    if not marked or not arming(early, full):
532:        return "unarmed"
533:    if not alive:
534:        return "dead"
535:    cpsr = dumped(late, cpsr_at)
536:    if cpsr is None or cpsr == POISON:
537:        return "nofire"
538:    got = "m=%02x" % (cpsr & 0x1F)
539:    if pin_if:
540:        got += " if=%d" % ((cpsr >> 6) & 3)
541:    if sp_at is not None:
542:        v = dumped(late, sp_at)
543:        #  #562 pass 2: ` sp0' is an ACTUAL zero readback (a never-loaded bank), not merely
544:        #  "not BOOT_SP" -- a missing or POISON slot now renders neither token.
545:        if v == BOOT_SP:
546:            got += " sp"
547:        elif v == 0:
548:            got += " sp0"
549:    t = early + late
550:    if (announced(t, once_key) if once_key else "(once)" in t):
551:        got += " once"
552:    if declines:
553:        for key, tag in (("msr_imm", "msr"), ("arm_pop", "pop"), ("dpi S-to-pc", "dpi")):
554:            if announced(t, key):
555:                got += " " + tag
556:    if backstops:
557:        if announced(t, "arm_save_register_bank"):
558:            got += " save"
559:        if announced(t, "arm_load_register_bank"):
560:            got += " load"
561:    if rt_at is not None:
562:        v = dumped(late, rt_at)
563:        if v not in (None, POISON) and (v & 0x1F) == 0x13:
564:            got += " rt"
565:    return got
566:
567:
568:def report_dead(why):
569:    print("arm_msrmode_probe -- binary=%s label=%s machine=testarm" % (BIN, LABEL))
570:    print("ARMMSRMODE_CONTROL=DEAD")
571:    print("ARMMSRMODE_RESULT=0/0")
572:    print("  *** SETUP FAILED (%s) -- the vehicle is not the vehicle.  NOT 'no defect'. ***" % why)
573:    for nm, got, want, note in rows:
574:        print("  %-11s got=%-16s want=%-16s %s" % (nm, got, want, note[:56]))
575:    print("ARMMSRMODE_DONE")
576:    raise SystemExit(0)
577:
578:
579:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- enc ok  (no guest)
580:#  MSR immediate:  cond 00110 R 10 field(19:16) 1111 rot(11:8) imm8.  The field nibble is
581:#  bits 19:16 and a mask cannot substitute for it (0x0FB0F000 kills bit 0x08 and cannot tell
582:#  the c-form from the f-form).
583:bad = []
584:for k, w in WORDS.items():
585:    if k.startswith("c_"):
586:        if ((w >> 16) & 0xF) != 0b0001 or (w & 0xFF) != int(k[2:], 16) \
587:                or ((w >> 8) & 0xF) != 0 or (w & 0x00400000) or (w & 0x0FB0F000) != 0x0320F000:
588:            bad.append(k)
589:    if k == "f_14":
590:        if ((w >> 16) & 0xF) != 0b1000 or (w & 0xFF) != 0x14 or ((w >> 8) & 0xF) != 0 \
591:                or (w & 0x00400000) or (w & 0x0FB0F000) != 0x0320F000:
592:            bad.append(k)
593:    if k.startswith("s_"):
594:        #  #562: the SPSR form -- same frame, field nibble 0001, bit 22 (R) SET.
595:        if ((w >> 16) & 0xF) != 0b0001 or (w & 0xFF) != int(k[2:], 16) \
596:                or ((w >> 8) & 0xF) != 0 or not (w & 0x00400000) \
597:                or (w & 0x0FB0F000) != 0x0320F000:
598:            bad.append(k)
599:    if k == "movs_pc_lr":
600:        #  data-processing MOV (opcode 1101), S set, Rd = 15, Rm = 14, no shift
601:        if (w >> 21) & 0xF != 0xD or not (w >> 20) & 1 or (w >> 12) & 0xF != 15 \
602:                or w & 0xFFF != 14 or (w >> 25) & 7 != 0:
603:            bad.append(k)
604:    if k in ("ldm_r6_pc_s", "mov_lr_8100", "add_lr_40", "sf_c0"):
605:        #  #562 pass 2: whole-word field decode against the intended operation.
606:        ok = {"ldm_r6_pc_s": (w >> 25) & 7 == 0b100 and (w >> 20) & 1 and (w >> 22) & 1
607:              and not (w >> 21) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 6 and w & 0xFFFF == 0x8000,
608:              "mov_lr_8100": (w >> 25) & 7 == 1 and (w >> 21) & 0xF == 0xD
609:              and not (w >> 20) & 1 and (w >> 12) & 0xF == 14
610:              and (((w & 0xFF) >> (2 * ((w >> 8) & 0xF))) | ((w & 0xFF)
611:                   << (32 - 2 * ((w >> 8) & 0xF)))) & 0xFFFFFFFF == TGT,
612:              "add_lr_40": (w >> 25) & 7 == 1 and (w >> 21) & 0xF == 0x4
613:              and not (w >> 20) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 14 and (w >> 12) & 0xF == 14
614:              and w & 0xFFF == 0x40,
615:              "sf_c0": (w & 0x0FB0F000) == 0x0320F000 and (w & 0x00400000)
616:              and ((w >> 16) & 0xF) == 0b1000 and ((w >> 8) & 0xF) == 1 and (w & 0xFF) == 3,
617:              }[k]
618:        if not ok:
619:            bad.append(k)
620:    if k in ("sf_ff", "ss_ff", "sx_ff", "cf_0", "msr_fsxc_r0", "msr_fsxc_r1", "adds_r0_pc_0",
621:             "ldm_r5_r0_s", "subs_pc_lr_0"):
622:        #  #562 repair 4: decode the closure words field by field (rotated imm value, R, field mask,
623:        #  opcode/S/Rn/Rd, LDM bits) against the operation each key names.
624:        rot = (w >> 8) & 0xF
625:        val = ((w & 0xFF) >> (2 * rot) | (w & 0xFF) << (32 - 2 * rot)) & 0xFFFFFFFF
626:        msri = (w & 0x0FB0F000) == 0x0320F000
627:        ok = {"sf_ff": msri and (w >> 22) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 8 and val == 0xFF000000,
628:              "ss_ff": msri and (w >> 22) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 4 and val == 0x00FF0000,
629:              "sx_ff": msri and (w >> 22) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 2 and val == 0x0000FF00,
630:              "cf_0": msri and not (w >> 22) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 0xE and val == 0,
631:              "msr_fsxc_r0": w & 0x0FFFFFF0 == 0x012FF000 and w & 0xF == 0,
632:              "msr_fsxc_r1": w & 0x0FFFFFF0 == 0x012FF000 and w & 0xF == 1,
633:              "adds_r0_pc_0": (w >> 25) & 7 == 1 and (w >> 21) & 0xF == 4 and (w >> 20) & 1
634:              and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 15 and (w >> 12) & 0xF == 0 and val == 0,
635:              "subs_pc_lr_0": (w >> 25) & 7 == 1 and (w >> 21) & 0xF == 2 and (w >> 20) & 1
636:              and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 14 and (w >> 12) & 0xF == 15 and val == 0,
637:              "ldm_r5_r0_s": (w >> 25) & 7 == 4 and (w >> 20) & 1 and (w >> 22) & 1
638:              and not (w >> 21) & 1 and (w >> 23) & 1 and not (w >> 24) & 1
639:              and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 5 and w & 0xFFFF == 0x0001}[k]
640:        if not ok or w >> 28 != 0xE:
641:            bad.append(k)
642:    if k in ("movs_pc_r5", "add_r5_40", "ldm_r6w_pc_s", "ldm_r5_pc", "add_pc_r6_0", "add_r0_pc_0",
643:             "str_r0_c", "str_r3_10", "str_r3_14"):
644:        #  #562 repair 3: cond, class, opcode, S/W/L, Rn, Rd and operand, field by field.
645:        f = ((w >> 28), (w >> 25) & 7, (w >> 21) & 0xF, (w >> 20) & 1, (w >> 16) & 0xF,
646:             (w >> 12) & 0xF, w & 0xFFF)
647:        want = {"movs_pc_r5": (0xE, 0, 0xD, 1, 0, 15, 5),
648:                "add_r5_40": (0xE, 1, 0x4, 0, 5, 5, 0x40),
649:                "add_pc_r6_0": (0xE, 1, 0x4, 0, 6, 15, 0),
650:                "add_r0_pc_0": (0xE, 1, 0x4, 0, 15, 0, 0),
651:                "str_r0_c": (0xE, 2, 0xC, 0, 4, 0, 0xC),
652:                "str_r3_10": (0xE, 2, 0xC, 0, 4, 3, 0x10),
653:                "str_r3_14": (0xE, 2, 0xC, 0, 4, 3, 0x14)}.get(k)
654:        if k == "ldm_r6w_pc_s":
655:            ok = (w >> 25) & 7 == 4 and (w >> 20) & 1 and (w >> 22) & 1 and (w >> 21) & 1 \
656:                and (w >> 23) & 1 and not (w >> 24) & 1 and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 6 \
657:                and w & 0xFFFF == 0x8000
658:        elif k == "ldm_r5_pc":
659:            ok = (w >> 25) & 7 == 4 and (w >> 20) & 1 and not (w >> 22) & 1 \
660:                and not (w >> 21) & 1 and (w >> 23) & 1 and not (w >> 24) & 1 \
661:                and (w >> 16) & 0xF == 5 and w & 0xFFFF == 0x8000
662:        else:
663:            ok = f == want
664:        if not ok:
665:            bad.append(k)
666:    if k == "ldm_r5_pc_s":
667:        #  LDM: bits 27:25 = 100, L set, S (bit 22) set, W clear, Rn = 5, list = {pc} only
668:        if (w >> 25) & 7 != 0b100 or not (w >> 20) & 1 or not (w >> 22) & 1 \
669:                or (w >> 21) & 1 or (w >> 16) & 0xF != 5 or w & 0xFFFF != 0x8000:
670:            bad.append(k)
671:row("enc ok", "clean" if not bad else ",".join(bad), "clean",
672:    "CONTROL=DEAD. Decoder match on the PLANTED literals: MSR-imm frame (w & 0x0FB0F000) == "
673:    "0x0320F000, field nibble (w>>16)&0xF = 0001 c-form / 1000 f-form, rot 0, bit 22 clear, imm8 "
674:    "== the key's mode.")
675:if bad:
676:    report_dead("enc ok")
677:
678:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S1: live / pc adv
679:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(
680:    prologue() + plant(["mov_r0_2a", "str_r0"])
681:    + ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step 2", dumpcmd(DEST), "print pc"])
682:row("live", "0x%x" % (dumped(early, DEST) or 0) if alive else "dead", "0x2a",
683:    "CONTROL=DEAD. Plant, step and dump executed at all.")
684:row("pc adv", "0x%x" % (printed(early, "pc") or 0) if alive else "dead", "0x%x" % (CODE + 8),
685:    "CONTROL=DEAD. The words were translated as 4-byte ARM instructions.")
686:if rows[-2][1] != rows[-2][2] or rows[-1][1] != rows[-1][2]:
687:    report_dead("live/pc adv")
688:
689:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S1b: armed
690:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(
691:    prologue() + plant(["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"])
692:    + ["pc=0x%x" % CODE, "step 3", dumpcmd(DEST, DEST + 8)])
693:a4, a8 = dumped(early, DEST + 4), dumped(early, DEST + 8)
694:armed = "%s/%s" % (("0x%x" % a4) if (alive and a4 is not None) else "?",
695:                   ("0x%x" % a8) if (alive and a8 is not None) else "?")
696:row("armed", armed, "0x%x/0x%x" % (BOOT_CPSR, BOOT_SP),
697:    "CONTROL=DEAD. SVC32 privileged testarm -- not USR32, not barearm, and not a debugger cpsr "
698:    "write. If this reds NO kill row may be scored.")
699:if armed != rows[-1][2]:
700:    report_dead("armed")
701:
702:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S2: no cbit
703:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["f_14", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [4])
704:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
705:row("no cbit", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8), "m=13 sp",
706:    "MSR CPSR_f writes the FLAGS byte, so the mode field is untouched and the host must live. "
707:    "NOT CONTROL=DEAD: a red here is a decoder finding, not a reproduction.")
708:
709:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S3/S4: the kill rows
710:for nm, key, dec in (("kill 14", "c_14", 20), ("kill 15", "c_15", 21)):
711:    cmds, full = msr_cmds([key, "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [1, 3])
712:    early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
713:    row(nm, classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, once_key="msr_imm",
714:                     pin_if=True), "m=13 if=0 sp once",
715:        "MSR CPSR_c, #0x%02x into a RESERVED mode reaches arm_load_register_bank's default: and "
716:        "exit(1)s. PRE is `dead' -- EOF ALONE -- and that FAIL is the reproduction. #562: "
717:        "if=0 pins FIELD-ONLY (the write clears I/F; a whole-op decline keeps if=3)."
718:        % int(key[2:], 16))
719:    t = early + late
720:    diagnosis.append("%s: %s" % (nm, "load mode %d seen" % dec
721:                                 if ("arm_load_register_bank: unimplemented mode %d" % dec) in t
722:                                 else "NO LOAD TEXT"))
723:
724:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S5: save 2s
725:#  R3: the spec's slots -- post-MSR1 CPSR at DEST+4, return CPSR at DEST+8, SP at DEST+12.
726:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_14", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "c_13", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_8", "str_sp_c"],
727:                      [1, 2, 1, 3])
728:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
729:row("save 2s", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 12, rt_at=DEST + 8),
730:    "m=13 sp once rt",
731:    "#0x14 then #0x13 in one process. On HEAD it dies on the FIRST MSR (the same Load death as "
732:    "kill 14). A Load-only fix still dies on the SECOND (Save of the reserved mode). Keep kill 15.")
733:t = early + late
734:diagnosis.append("save 2s: load=%s save=%s" % (
735:    "yes" if "arm_load_register_bank: unimplemented mode 20" in t else "no",
736:    "yes" if "arm_save_register_bank: unimplemented mode 20" in t else "no"))
737:
738:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S6..S13: accept side
739:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_10", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [4])
740:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
741:row("acc usr", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8), "m=10 sp0",
742:    "USR32 is ONE-WAY (the USR mask strips the c-byte). SP is the USR bank's (0), so ` sp' in "
743:    "the got means the bank Load did not happen.")
744:
745:for nm, key, want_m in (("acc fiq", "c_11", 0x11), ("acc irq", "c_12", 0x12),
746:                        ("acc abt", "c_17", 0x17), ("acc und", "c_1b", 0x1B),
747:                        ("acc sys", "c_1f", 0x1F)):
748:    cmds, full = msr_cmds([key, "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8",
749:                           "c_13", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_c", "str_sp_10"], [8],
750:                          late_end=DEST + 16)
751:    early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
752:    if not marked or not arming(early, full):
753:        got = "unarmed"
754:    elif not alive:
755:        got = "dead"
756:    else:
757:        arrive, sp_arr = dumped(late, DEST + 4), dumped(late, DEST + 8)
758:        back, sp_back = dumped(late, DEST + 12), dumped(late, DEST + 16)
759:        got = "%s/%s/%s/%s" % (
760:            "m=%02x" % (arrive & 0x1F) if arrive not in (None, POISON) else "nofire",
761:            "0" if sp_arr == 0 else "x",
762:            "m=%02x" % (back & 0x1F) if back not in (None, POISON) else "nofire",
763:            "sp" if sp_back == BOOT_SP else "nosp")
764:    row(nm, got, "m=%02x/0/m=13/sp" % want_m,
765:        "ACCEPT + CANARY in one row: arrive mode/SP==0 (banked, BSS-zero), return mode 0x13 with "
766:        "SP==BOOT_SP. A Save no-op returns SP=0; a Load no-op arrives with SP=BOOT_SP.")
767:
768:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_13", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [4])
769:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
770:row("same svc", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8), "m=13 sp",
771:    "SAME-MODE: Load is not called, so SP-UNCHANGED *IS* the preservation check. Not 0xd3 -- "
772:    "#0x13 clears I|F.")
773:
774:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_10", "c_14", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4"], [4])
775:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
776:row("usr mask", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full), "m=10",
777:    "In USR32 the c-byte is STRIPPED, so the following #0x14 must NOT reach the mode field. "
778:    "The host lives and the mode stays 0x10.")
779:
780:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 rows
781:#  kill 1e: pins the helper's DOMAIN past the two driven reserved values -- a range form
782:#  admitting 0x1c-0x1e sends 0x1e to Load's backstop and reads m=1e.
783:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_1e", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [1, 3])
784:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
785:row("kill 1e", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, once_key="msr_imm",
786:                        pin_if=True), "m=13 if=0 sp once",
787:    "MSR CPSR_c, #0x1e: unmodelled, like 0x14/0x15. Kills a helper widened by RANGE to 0x1e.")
788:diag_unimpl("kill 1e", early + late)
789:
790:#  kill 03: the only driven mode value with bit 4 CLEAR.  Every other MSR value here has bit 4
791:#  set, so a decline that cleared only M[3:0] from the mask (`& ~0x0f') still wrote bit 4 = 0 from
792:#  this value and reached Load's backstop with mode 0x03; the rows before this one could not see it.
793:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_03", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [1, 3])
794:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
795:row("kill 03", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, once_key="msr_imm",
796:                        pin_if=True), "m=13 if=0 sp once",
797:    "MSR CPSR_c, #0x03 (bit 4 clear): declined, mode unchanged. Pins the full 5-bit mode mask.")
798:diag_unimpl("kill 03", early + late)
799:
800:#  The two SPSR restores.  `MSR SPSR_c, #0x14' poisons spsr_svc (I=F=0, mode 0x14); the restore
801:#  must land at TGT (else `nofire') in SVC32 -- current mode kept -- with I/F FROM THE SPSR
802:#  (if=0; a restore that skipped the CPSR write keeps the boot if=3) and the SVC SP.
803:for nm, op, site in (("rst movs", "movs_pc_lr", "dpi S-to-pc"),
804:                     ("rst ldm", "ldm_r5_pc_s", "arm_pop")):
805:    cmds, full = msr_cmds(["s_14", op], [6], restore=True)
806:    early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
807:    row(nm, classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, once_key=site,
808:                     pin_if=True), "m=13 if=0 sp once",
809:        "MSR SPSR_c,#0x14 then %s: the restore reaches Load's default: (HEAD dead). Post-fix: "
810:        "at TGT, mode kept, I/F from the SPSR, `%s' announce." % (op, site))
811:    diag_unimpl(nm, early + late)
812:
813:#  zero spsr: NO MSR at all -- spsr_svc is never written on testarm (cpu_new zero-fills), so
814:#  `MOVS pc,lr' from boot SVC32 restores mode 0x00.
815:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["movs_pc_lr"], [4], restore=True)
816:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
817:row("zero spsr", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8,
818:                          once_key="dpi S-to-pc", pin_if=True), "m=13 if=0 sp once",
819:    "MOVS pc,lr from boot SVC32 with spsr_svc never written (mode 0x00). HEAD dead.")
820:diag_unimpl("zero spsr", early + late)
821:
822:#  The restores' ACCEPT side: a modelled SPSR mode must be APPLIED.  A guard made unconditional
823:#  (always keep the current mode) reads m=13 here.  SYS32 SP is the usr/sys bank's (0).
824:for nm, op in (("acc movs", "movs_pc_lr"), ("acc ldm", "ldm_r5_pc_s")):
825:    cmds, full = msr_cmds(["s_1f", op], [6], restore=True)
826:    early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
827:    row(nm, classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, pin_if=True),
828:        "m=1f if=0 sp0",
829:        "MSR SPSR_c,#0x1f then %s: SYS32 restored, SP from the usr/sys bank (0), no announce."
830:        % op)
831:
832:#  The BACKSTOPS: reached only with an unmodelled mode already in CPSR, which only the debugger
833:#  `cpsr=' ASSIGNMENT can now install (no bank switch, no flags
834:#  sync).  NOT `put', which writes MEMORY.  The poke follows the arming dumps.  once_key names
835:#  a DECLINE site that must NOT announce: a plant is not a guest decline (dbg both: the DPI
836:#  guard runs only when an SPSR was copied, and mode 0x14 has none).
837:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_13", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"], [4], poke=["cpsr=0xd4"])
838:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
839:row("dbg save", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, backstops=True,
840:                         once_key="msr_imm"),
841:    "m=13 sp0 save",
842:    "cpsr=0xd4 then MSR CPSR_c,#0x13: Save's default: (HEAD exit(1)) announces and returns; "
843:    "Load(SVC) gives the never-saved svc SP: an actual 0, ` sp0'.")
844:diag_unimpl("dbg save", early + late)
845:
846:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["movs_pc_lr"], [4], restore=True, poke=["cpsr=0xd4"])
847:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
848:row("dbg both", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, backstops=True,
849:                         once_key="dpi S-to-pc"),
850:    "m=14 sp save load",
851:    "cpsr=0xd4 then MOVS pc,lr: no SPSR for 0x14, so BOTH Save's and Load's default: run in ONE "
852:    "instruction (Load's backstop and the distinct bits are ALSO carried by latch rpt).")
853:diag_unimpl("dbg both", early + late)
854:
855:#  latch ind: ALL THREE guest declines in ONE process -- MSR CPSR_c,#0x14, then MSR SPSR_c,#0x14
856:#  and LDM {pc}^ (arm_pop) to TGT, whose MOVS pc,lr (DPI) restores the same poisoned spsr_svc to
857:#  TGT2.  Each site has its own mode_warned bit, so all three texts must appear; any two sharing a
858:#  bit print only the first.  (The other rows are each a fresh process and cannot see sharing.)
859:cmds, full = msr_cmds(["c_14", "s_14", "ldm_r5_pc_s"], [8], restore=True, chain=True)
860:early, late, alive, marked = _session_split(cmds)
861:#  once_key="register_bank": the generic ` once' token would be set by ANY of the three texts and
862:#  so carries nothing here; keyed on the backstops it pins their ABSENCE instead (no guest
863:#  decline may fall through to Save/Load).  The per-site ` msr pop dpi' tags are the channel.
864:row("latch ind", classify(early, late, alive, marked, full, sp_at=DEST + 8, pin_if=True,
865:                          once_key="register_bank", declines=True), "m=13 if=0 sp msr pop dpi",
866:    "MSR, LDM^ and MOVS declines in ONE session: three distinct latch bits, three texts.")
867:diag_unimpl("latch ind", early + late)
868:
869:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 pass 2: latch rpt
870:#  EVERY one of the five latch sites visited TWICE in ONE process.  Wants EXACTLY ONE announce per
871:#  site (a latch that never suppresses prints two; two sites sharing a bit print one between
872:#  them) AND the repair still applied on the second visit: the declines leave SVC32 (a=13/..),
873:#  the backstops leave the planted 0x14 alive (b=14/..).
874:#    CODE  c_14 c_15 (msr x2)  s_14  ldm r5 -> T1      T1  ldm r6 -> T2  (pop x2)
875:#    T2    movs pc,lr -> T3                            T3  add lr,#0x40 ; movs -> T4  (dpi x2)
876:#    T4    mrs ; str [r4,#4] ; str sp,[r4,#8]
877:#  then cpsr=0xd4, pc=T5, lr=T6:
878:#    T5    movs pc,lr -> T6  (save+load)   T6  add lr,#0x40 ; movs -> T7  (save+load again)
879:#    T7    mrs ; str [r4,#12] ; str sp,[r4,#16]
880:LR1, LR2, LR3, LR4, LR5, LR6, LR7 = 0x8100, 0x8140, 0x8180, 0x81C0, 0x8200, 0x8240, 0x8280
881:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
882:    ["c_14", "c_15", "s_14", "ldm_r5_pc_s"],
883:    blocks=[(LR1, ["ldm_r6_pc_s"]), (LR2, ["movs_pc_lr"]), (LR3, ["add_lr_40", "movs_pc_lr"]),
884:            (LR4, ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "str_sp_8"]), (LR5, ["movs_pc_lr"]),
885:            (LR6, ["add_lr_40", "movs_pc_lr"]), (LR7, ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_c", "str_sp_10"])],
886:    data={LDMW: LR1, LDMW + 4: LR2},
887:    regs=["r5=0x%x" % LDMW, "r6=0x%x" % (LDMW + 4), "lr=0x%x" % LR3],
888:    segments=(((), 11), (["cpsr=0xd4", "pc=0x%x" % LR5, "lr=0x%x" % LR6], 6)),
889:    late_end=DEST + 16)
890:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
891:    got = "unarmed"
892:elif not alive:
893:    got = "dead"
894:else:
895:    def _half(ca, sa):
896:        c, v = dumped(late, ca), dumped(late, sa)
897:        if c in (None, POISON):
898:            return "nofire"
899:        return "%02x/%d/%s" % (c & 0x1F, (c >> 6) & 3,
900:                               "sp" if v == BOOT_SP else ("0" if v == 0 else "x"))
901:    t = early + late
902:    got = "a=%s b=%s msr%d pop%d dpi%d save%d load%d" % (
903:        _half(DEST + 4, DEST + 8), _half(DEST + 12, DEST + 16),
904:        announces(t, "msr_imm"), announces(t, "arm_pop"), announces(t, "dpi S-to-pc"),
905:        announces(t, "arm_save_register_bank"), announces(t, "arm_load_register_bank"))
906:row("latch rpt", got, "a=13/0/sp b=14/3/sp msr1 pop1 dpi1 save1 load1",
907:    "Five latch sites x2 in ONE process: exactly one announce each, repair kept on visit 2.")
908:diag_unimpl("latch rpt", early + late)
909:
910:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 repair 3: src dpi / src pop
911:#  CLASS CLOSURE of label x latch x outcome x masked bits (see the header).  Per label and path,
912:#  ONE process, four chained restores, each read back:
913:#    enter the label with I|F set; SPSR := N|Z|0xdf; restore     -> ACCEPT, latch clear  (R1)
914:#    re-enter it with I|F CLEAR;  SPSR_c := 0xcf;   restore     -> DECLINE, latch clear (R2)
915:#                                                    restore     -> DECLINE, latch SET   (R3)
916:#                                 SPSR_c := 0xdf;   restore     -> ACCEPT, latch set    (R4)
917:#  DPI chains through `movs pc,r5' (lr is banked; r5 is not) with r5 += 0x40 per block; POP chains
918:#  through `ldmia r6!,{pc}^' over a table of block addresses.  Want R1 = R4 = ffffffdf and R2 = R3
919:#  = ffffffc0|label (mode kept, every other bit from the SPSR 0xffffffcf; `msr cpsr_fsx,#0' and the
920:#  label re-entry before each decline leave the old CPSR 0x0000000m), and EXACTLY ONE announce.
921:BLK = [TGT + 0x40 * i for i in range(4)]     # 0x8100 0x8140 0x8180 0x81c0
922:for lab, mode in (("fiq", 0x11), ("irq", 0x12), ("abt", 0x17), ("und", 0x1B), ("svc", 0x13)):
923:    ck = "c_%02x" % (0xC0 | mode)            # first entry: I|F SET (helper operand bits 7:6)
924:    cc = "c_%02x" % mode                     # re-entry: I|F CLEAR, so the declines' I/F (set in
925:                                             # the SPSR) can only have come from the SPSR
926:    for path in ("dpi", "pop"):
927:        if path == "dpi":
928:            early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
929:                [ck, "sf_ff", "ss_ff", "sx_ff", "s_df", "movs_pc_r5"],
930:                blocks=[(BLK[0], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "add_r5_40", "cf_0", cc, "s_cf",
931:                                  "movs_pc_r5"]),
932:                        (BLK[1], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_8", "add_r5_40", "cf_0", cc, "movs_pc_r5"]),
933:                        (BLK[2], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_c", "add_r5_40", "s_df", "movs_pc_r5"]),
934:                        (BLK[3], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_10"])],
935:                regs=["r5=0x%x" % BLK[0]],
936:                segments=(((), 26),), late_end=DEST + 0x14)
937:            key = "dpi S-to-pc"
938:        else:
939:            early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
940:                [ck, "sf_ff", "ss_ff", "sx_ff", "s_df", "ldm_r6w_pc_s"],
941:                blocks=[(BLK[0], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "cf_0", cc, "s_cf", "ldm_r6w_pc_s"]),
942:                        (BLK[1], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_8", "cf_0", cc, "ldm_r6w_pc_s"]),
943:                        (BLK[2], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_c", "s_df", "ldm_r6w_pc_s"]),
944:                        (BLK[3], ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_10"])],
945:                data={LDMW + 4 * i: BLK[i] for i in range(4)},
946:                regs=["r6=0x%x" % LDMW],
947:                segments=(((), 23),), late_end=DEST + 0x14)
948:            key = "arm_pop"
949:        if not marked or not arming(early, full):
950:            got = "unarmed"
951:        elif not alive:
952:            got = "dead"
953:        else:
954:            vals = [dumped(late, DEST + o) for o in (4, 8, 12, 16)]
955:            got = " ".join("nofire" if v in (None, POISON) else "%08x" % v for v in vals) \
956:                + " n=%d" % announces(early + late, key)
957:        acc, dec = 0xFFFFFFDF, 0xFFFFFFC0 | mode
958:        row("src %s %s" % (path, lab), got, "%08x %08x %08x %08x n=1" % (acc, dec, dec, acc),
959:            "%s from %s: accept, decline, decline (latch set), accept; one announce."
960:            % (path.upper(), lab.upper()))
961:        diag_unimpl("src %s %s" % (path, lab), early + late)
962:
963:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 repair 3: msr lbl
964:#  The msr_imm guard at every current-mode label it can run in (USR strips the c-byte): enter
965:#  FIQ, IRQ, ABT, UND, SYS in turn WITH I|F set, and in each write #0x14.  Each decline keeps the
966:#  label and clears I/F (the c-byte 0x14 has them clear).  One announce in total.
967:seq, blocks = [], []
968:for i, m in enumerate((0x11, 0x12, 0x17, 0x1B, 0x1F)):
969:    seq += ["c_%02x" % (0xC0 | m), "c_14", "mrs_r3", ("str_r3_4", "str_r3_8", "str_r3_c",
970:                                                      "str_r3_10", "str_r3_14")[i]]
971:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(seq, segments=(((), 20),), late_end=DEST + 0x14)
972:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
973:    got = "unarmed"
974:elif not alive:
975:    got = "dead"
976:else:
977:    vals = [dumped(late, DEST + o) for o in (4, 8, 12, 16, 20)]
978:    got = " ".join("nofire" if v in (None, POISON) else "%02x" % v for v in vals) \
979:        + " n=%d" % announces(early + late, "msr_imm")
980:row("msr lbl", got, "11 12 17 1b 1f n=1",
981:    "MSR CPSR_c,#0x14 from FIQ IRQ ABT UND SYS: declined at every label, one announce.")
982:diag_unimpl("msr lbl", early + late)
983:
984:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 repair 3: encl
985:#  The restores' ENCLOSING predicates.  SVC with spsr_svc = 0x1f (a VALID, different mode), then
986:#  three PC writes that must NOT restore it: a plain `ldmia r5,{pc}' (return_flag 0), a non-S
987:#  `add pc,r6,#0' (the A__PC template instance, not the `ret' shortcut that `mov pc,lr' decodes
988:#  to), and `add r0,pc,#0' (Rn = PC, Rd != PC: no PC write at all).  Wants m=13 after each and
989:#  r0 = its own address + 8.
990:E1, E2 = TGT, TGT + 0x40
991:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
992:    ["s_1f", "ldm_r5_pc"],
993:    blocks=[(E1, ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "add_pc_r6_0"]),
994:            (E2, ["add_r0_pc_0", "str_r0_c", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_8"])],
995:    data={LDMW: E1}, regs=["r5=0x%x" % LDMW, "r6=0x%x" % E2],
996:    segments=(((), 9),), late_end=DEST + 0x10)
997:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
998:    got = "unarmed"
999:elif not alive:
1000:    got = "dead"
1001:else:
1002:    m1, m2, r0 = dumped(late, DEST + 4), dumped(late, DEST + 8), dumped(late, DEST + 12)
1003:    got = " ".join("nofire" if v in (None, POISON) else f(v)
1004:                   for v, f in ((m1, lambda x: "%02x" % (x & 0x1F)),
1005:                                (m2, lambda x: "%02x" % (x & 0x1F)), (r0, lambda x: "%x" % x)))
1006:row("encl", got, "13 13 %x" % (E2 + 8),
1007:    "Plain LDM {pc}, non-S ADD pc, ADD r0,pc with spsr_svc = 0x1f: none may restore the SPSR.")
1008:
1009:T2, T3, T4, T5 = 0x8200, 0x8300, 0x8340, 0x8380
1010:T6 = 0x83C0
1011:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
1012:    ["s_3f", "ldm_r5_pc_s"],
1013:    blocks=[(TGT, []), (T2, ["s_3f", "movs_pc_lr"]), (T3, ["c_3f"]), (T4, ["c_34"]),
1014:            (T5, ["s_34", "ldm_r5_pc_s"]), (T6, ["s_34", "movs_pc_lr"])],
1015:    data={LDMW: TGT}, regs=["r5=0x%x" % LDMW, "lr=0x%x" % TGT],
1016:    segments=(((), 2), (["print cpsr", "cpsr=0xd3", "pc=0x%x" % T2, "lr=0x%x" % TGT], 2),
1017:              (["print cpsr", "cpsr=0xd3", "pc=0x%x" % T3], 1),
1018:              (["print cpsr", "cpsr=0xd3", "pc=0x%x" % T4], 1),
1019:              (["print cpsr", "cpsr=0xd3", "pc=0x%x" % T5], 2),
1020:              (["print cpsr", "cpsr=0xd3", "pc=0x%x" % T6, "lr=0x%x" % TGT], 2),
1021:              (["print cpsr"], 0)))
1022:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
1023:    got = "unarmed"
1024:elif not alive:
1025:    got = "dead"
1026:else:
1027:    vals = re.findall(r"print\s+cpsr\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)", late)
1028:    t = early + late
1029:    got = " ".join("%02x" % (int(v, 16) & 0xff) for v in vals) + " n=%d" % (
1030:        announces(t, "msr_imm") + announces(t, "arm_pop") + announces(t, "dpi S-to-pc"))
1031:row("tbit", got, "3f 3f 3f 33 33 33 n=3",
1032:    "T-set accept via pop/DPI/msr (0x3f), T-set decline via msr/pop/DPI (0x34): T from the operand.")
1033:T7 = 0x8400
1034:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
1035:    ["s_1f", "adds_r0_pc_0", "mov_r0_2a", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "ldm_r5_r0_s", "mrs_r3",
1036:     "str_r3_8", "s_14", "subs_pc_lr_0"],
1037:    blocks=[(T7, ["mrs_r3", "str_r3_c", "c_11", "c_03", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_10"])],
1038:    data={LDMW: 0x12345678}, regs=["r5=0x%x" % LDMW, "lr=0x%x" % T7],
1039:    segments=(((), 16),), late_end=DEST + 0x14)
1040:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
1041:    got = "unarmed"
1042:elif not alive:
1043:    got = "dead"
1044:else:
1045:    vals = [dumped(late, DEST + o) for o in (4, 8, 12, 16)]
1046:    got = " ".join("nofire" if v in (None, POISON) else "%02x" % (v & 0x1f) for v in vals)
1047:row("encl2", got, "13 13 13 11",
1048:    "adds r0,pc / ldm {r0}^ must not restore; subs pc,lr declines 0x14; msr #0x03 at FIQ declined.")
1049:#  msr wide: the msr_imm path's operand bits 31:8 (only the register form reaches them).  ACCEPT
1050:#  r0 = 0xffffffd1 (FIQ, every bit but T and mode bits 1-3): a widened helper projection declines
1051:#  it.  Then, from FIQ, DECLINE r1 = 0x00000014: field-only, so every non-mode bit comes from the
1052:#  operand -- bits 31:6 differ from the old CPSR -- and the mode stays FIQ: want 0x00000011.
1053:early, late, alive, marked, full = prog_session(
1054:    ["msr_fsxc_r0", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_4", "msr_fsxc_r1", "mrs_r3", "str_r3_8"],
1055:    regs=["r0=0xffffffd1", "r1=0x14"], segments=(((), 6),), late_end=DEST + 0x10)
1056:if not marked or not arming(early, full):
1057:    got = "unarmed"
1058:elif not alive:
1059:    got = "dead"
