1068:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- #562 repair 5: the GENERATED GRID
1069:#  Owner ruling 2026-10-08: the restore/MSR detector rows are GENERATED from the full space, not
1070:#  written by hand.  Three sessions (one per path: msr_imm, DPI S-to-PC, arm_pop), each a list of
1071:#  OBSERVATIONS produced by grid_obs() below.  One observation:
1072:#      debugger:  cpsr=0xd3 (re-arm; a previous result may have T set), pc=<block>, r0=OLD, r1=NEW
1073:#      guest:     msr cpsr_fsxc,r0           -- OLD CPSR, a modelled label, set by a real MSR
1074:#                                               (bank switch and `flags' both correct)
1075:#                 msr spsr_fsxc,r1           -- (restore paths only) SPSR := NEW
1076:#                 the instruction under test -- msr cpsr_fsxc,r1 / movs pc,r2 / ldmia r6,{pc}^
1077:#                                               (pop also: ldmia r6,{pc}, ldmia r6,{r0}^, ldmia r6,{r0})
1078:#      debugger:  print cpsr                 -- the WHOLE result word, compared exactly with WANT
1079:#  WANT is computed: accept -> NEW; decline -> (NEW & ~0x1f) | label; a non-restoring pop form
1080:#  -> OLD.  The first decline in a session runs with the site's latch CLEAR, every later one with
1081:#  it SET; the site must announce exactly once and no Save/Load backstop text may appear.
1082:#
1083:#  G1 per path x outcome x bit 0..31 x polarity: observations come in COMPLEMENTARY PAIRS --
1084:#     p1: OLD = label (bits 31:5 all 0)          NEW = 0xffffffe0 | mode (bits 31:5 all 1, T SET)
1085:#     p2: OLD = 0xffffffc0 | label (31:6 all 1)  NEW = mode (bits 31:5 all 0)
1086:#     so for every non-mode bit both result polarities are observed with the OLD value different
1087:#     (keep-old, force-0 and force-1 all change the word).  T cannot be 1 in OLD (the guest runs
1088:#     ARM code), so T polarity 0 is observed only with OLD T = 0 -- keep-old T is caught at p1.
1089:#  G2 MSR label x mode bit: each label also declines label ^ 0x1f, which differs in EVERY mode bit
1090:#     (and is always unmodelled, since bit 4 is cleared); on the restore paths the same value is
1091:#     the declined SPSR, so a keep-mode mask that lets any SPSR mode bit through changes the word.
1092:#  G3 helper boundary: ALL 25 unmodelled values (0x00-0x0f, 0x14-0x16, 0x18-0x1a, 0x1c-0x1e) are
1093:#     declined on EVERY path, labels cycling; ALL 7 modelled modes are accepted on every path.
1094:#     A narrowed projection (e.g. `& 0x17' admits 0x18-0x1a) or widened one changes some word.
1095:#  G4 pop enclosing cells: {S, non-S} x {PC, no PC} all four, both polarities.
1096:#  The `grid cov' row re-derives the bit x polarity table from the generated observations and
1097:#  reds if any cell outside the named equivalents is uncovered.
